Chapter: PropArithFalse

 Negative guard for arithmetic in a proposition. Folding `1 + 2 * 3`
 must give 7, so this claim of 9 is false and must be rejected.

 9 is not an arbitrary wrong answer. It is exactly what a single
 left-associative loop computes for `1 + 2 * 3`, so this file is the
 tripwire for the multiplicative level losing its precedence: if that
 regresses, this proof starts succeeding and the compiler proves a
 false theorem.

Section: Bad Proof

  claim wrong-grouping : 1 + 2 * 3 === 9
  proof wrong-grouping = Refl
  qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "unreachable"
  end
